    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite shows `BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 the project's only test class (`AcceptanceTest`, 2 tests) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field following the existing Spring/MapStruct conventions used for the other derived owner attributes.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` DTO schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), documenting the format and enumerated values.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/Regions.java`** \u2014 added `isKnownRegion(String)`, which reports whether a region code is one of the known regions (NSW/VIC/QLD) in the existing region-to-range table.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` plus a `formatOwnerSegment(Owner)` default method:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `formatMembershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when the owner's locality (`formatLocality`) is a known region, else `REGIONAL`.\n   - Returns `<TIER>_<AREA>`, or `null` only when the owner is `null` (consistent with the other mapper methods).\n\nThis reuses the already-established `formatMembershipLevel` and `formatLocality` helpers, so the segment stays consistent with the `membershipLevel` and `locality` fields in the same response.",
